  {"clause_id": "c016", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c017", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The exclusion of \"indirect, incidental or consequential damages\" runs in St. Jude's favour only and says nothing about Recipient, while Section 7 makes Recipient liable to indemnify \"any and all claims ... of any nature whatsoever.\" Whether the exclusion caps anything Recipient owes under Section 7 is left open.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c018", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The indemnity covers claims \"arising out of or related to Recipient's acceptance, use and disposal of the Materials\" with no carve-out for St. Jude's own negligence or willful misconduct, unlike the parties' 2003 agreement, which contained one. \"[R]elated to\" is also unbounded, leaving unclear whether claims about St. Jude's own conduct fall inside it.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c019", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The aggregate limit is written as \"Three Million ($1,000,000) dollars,\" so the words and the figures state different amounts. The required aggregate coverage cannot be determined from the provision as written.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.44}
